---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const repo = "https://github.com/taskinoz/Impression-Eyes-Reborn";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Impression Eyes Reborn"
  description="Privacy policy for Impression Eyes Reborn."
  footerText="Local images stay local."
  showFeaturesLink={false}
>
  <div class="legal wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy · 24 August 2026</p>
    <h1>Private by design.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Impression Eyes Reborn does not collect, store, sell or transmit personal data.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>What the app accesses</h2>
      <p>
        The app reads images that you explicitly open, drop onto it or browse from the same local
        folder. Image processing happens on your device. The app has no analytics, advertising,
        accounts or telemetry.
      </p>
      <h2>Network use</h2>
      <p>
        The image viewer itself does not make network requests. The GitHub installer offers a
        separate, default-off updater component. If you opt in, it checks the project's GitHub
        Releases page once per day and downloads a newer installer when one is available. It does
        not send image names, paths, usage information, installation IDs or device identifiers;
        GitHub receives ordinary connection information such as your IP address and updater user
        agent. Portable and Microsoft Store editions do not include this updater.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, open an issue on <a href={repo}>the project’s GitHub repository</a>.
        If data-handling features are added later, this policy will be updated before they are
        released.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
